<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Chad</h1><p class="st-meta">1960 CE – present · capital N'Djamena</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A landlocked Central African republic, independent from France in 1960, marked by civil wars and by the Déby family's rule since 1990.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chad-french-colony">French colony of Chad</a>, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-equatorial-africa">French Equatorial Africa</a>, was granted independence on 11 August 1960. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-tombalbaye">François Tombalbaye</a>, the leader of the Chadian Progressive Party and an ethnic Sara, became its first president, in a country of over 200 ethnic and linguistic groups.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1962 Tombalbaye banned opposition parties and set up a one-party system, and in 1965 Muslims in the north began a civil war. He was overthrown and killed in 1975. In 1979 rebel factions took the capital and central authority collapsed. Hissène Habré won the contest for power, expelled the Libyan army with French support in 1987, and ruled as a dictator, with thousands estimated killed under him. His general Idriss Déby overthrew him in 1990 and reintroduced multiparty politics. Oil exports began in 2003.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Déby died on 20 April 2021 after a rebel incursion from the north, and his son Mahamat Déby was named interim president by a Transitional Council of military officers. The council replaced the 2018 constitution with a charter. Mahamat Idriss Déby was sworn in as president on 23 May 2024 after a disputed election held on 6 May.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chad.jpg" alt="Chad" width="330" height="220"><figcaption>Image: SKopp &amp; others (see upload log) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1960 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>N'Djamena</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>François Tombalbaye, Hissène Habré, Idriss Déby, Mahamat Déby</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/chad">Chad</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Chad</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=chad" aria-label="Chad on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5094 1726 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chad lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5414 1982L5401 2038"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5401 2038h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5414 1982h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5414 1982h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks N'Djamena. <a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=chad">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
